Generate a cohesive family of full-bleed Urkaaaz Loadout unit-card
illustrations.

Create five separate images, one image-generation request per unit. Do not
combine the outputs into a grid, montage, contact sheet, collage, or sprite
sheet.

REFERENCE INPUTS

- Attach the previously supplied Loadout screenshot as the primary reference
  for the full-card character scale, painterly fantasy-game finish, and
  rich-but-readable treatment. Use it for visual direction only; do not copy
  its fictional units or exact card art.
- Attach each current Urkaaaz unit icon. These are the authoritative identity
  references for that unit's face, silhouette, armor, clothing, colors, and
  equipment. Preserve the recognizable design; do not redesign the unit.
- Attach the current main-menu background as the palette and atmosphere
  reference. Use its bright blue sky, warm cream clouds, golden sunlight,
  green landscape, and earthy materials as a shared color family. Do not
  reproduce the complete background composition inside every card.

ART DIRECTION

- Each image is a portrait, full-bleed illustration intended to fill one
  complete Loadout carousel card. The character must be much larger than the
  current small icon and remain immediately recognizable at mobile-card size.
- The unit does not need to keep the pose shown in its icon. Choose a new,
  expressive pose that fits the portrait composition and conveys the unit's
  personality; use the icon to preserve identity, not to copy its pose.
- Match the screenshot's polished painterly fantasy style: dimensional
  hand-painted forms, expressive character rendering, warm cinematic light,
  controlled saturation, clear silhouettes, and detailed but uncluttered
  materials.
- Keep all five illustrations visually cohesive in camera distance, character
  scale, lighting direction, contrast, detail density, and background palette.
- Use a soft-focus battlefield background inspired by the supplied main-menu
  background. Keep scenery subdued behind the character so each card feels
  connected to the home screen without competing with the unit.
- Compose for a narrow portrait card. Keep the face, defining equipment, and
  silhouette inside the central 80% of the image. Do not crop the head,
  hands, weapon, mount, or other defining features at the edges.
- Reserve the lower 22% for a darker, low-detail area so Android can overlay
  the unit name and availability status legibly. Keep the upper-right corner
  visually simple for the native information button.
- The art may fill the whole card, but the image itself must contain no card
  frame, border, selected outline, badge, text, or control. Android renders
  those layers separately.
- Do not add gameplay effects, props, equipment, faction marks, or unit
  abilities not visible in the supplied icon. The icon is the source of truth
  for the unit's identity and equipment, while pose, expression, and camera
  angle may be adapted to make a stronger card illustration.

OUTPUT FORMAT

- Produce exactly one independent PNG per unit, at exactly 512 x 720 pixels.
- Use full-bleed opaque backgrounds, portrait composition, and clean edges.
- Never include transparent checkerboards, empty margins, a tiled background,
  or a neighboring card in the output.
- Save generated files for review/staging under:
  `assets_src/loadout/unit-cards/`
- Do not copy generated images into Android resources until the user approves
  the reviewed previews.
- After approval, runtime resources belong under:
  `android-app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/`
- These are presentation illustrations only. Do not change battlefield
  sprites, animation frames, hitboxes, or gameplay balance.

OUTPUT FILES

1. `loadout_unit_defender_card.png` — `DEFENDER`; use the supplied Defender
   icon as the exact identity reference.
2. `loadout_unit_sapper_card.png` — `SAPPER`; use the supplied Sapper icon as
   the exact identity reference.
3. `loadout_unit_demolisher_card.png` — `DEMOLISHER`; use the supplied
   Demolisher icon as the exact identity reference.
4. `loadout_unit_raging_boar_card.png` — `RAGING_BOAR`; preserve the exact
   goblin-and-boar identity from the supplied icon.
5. `loadout_unit_slingmaster_card.png` — `SLINGMASTER`; preserve the exact
   goblin identity and sling equipment from the supplied icon.

MUST-HAVE VALIDATION BEFORE DELIVERY

- Verify exactly five independent files exist and filenames match the list.
- Verify every file is a valid PNG with dimensions exactly 512 x 720.
- Preview each image at the actual narrow Loadout-card aspect ratio and at a
  small mobile display size.
- Confirm each character is recognizable against its supplied icon and that
  no defining feature is clipped or obscured by the reserved UI areas.
- Compare all five images as one set for consistent character scale, lighting,
  painterly rendering, contrast, and main-menu-inspired palette.
- Confirm the images contain no text, UI, card frame, badge, watermark,
  signature, unrelated character, unsupported equipment, or gameplay effect.
- Reject and regenerate any output that fails validation. Show the previews
  for approval before Android integration.

NEGATIVE PROMPT

text, letters, numbers, logos, watermark, signature, UI, HUD, item name,
availability label, information icon, selection checkmark, selected border,
card frame, rivets, badge, stat symbols, price, inventory count, transparent
checkerboard, blank border, cropped face, cropped defining equipment, tiny
character, distant group, multiple units, unrelated unit, redesigned armor,
invented weapon, invented gameplay ability, unsupported magical aura,
photorealism, flat vector art, low contrast, noisy background, unrelated
franchise, copied screenshot character, pose copied from identity icon,
collage, contact sheet, sprite sheet
